  "interpretation": "At these four selected source-image ROIs, the worker reconstruction had lower mean absolute channel error to the known pre-JPEG logical source than GDI+/WIC in each case: high-entropy 44.75 vs 47.26; vertical edge 32.67 vs 52.73; horizontal edge 32.67 vs 52.70; checker 0.50 vs 36.67. GDI+ and WIC match at the selected points, and the worker matches pinned jpeg-js over the full frame, but neither comparison establishes JPEG ground truth or codec independence. This is one sample per selected ROI and a synthetic lossy encoder fixture; it does not establish general decoder correctness, a whole-image error rate, or a 4:2:0 acceptance threshold.",
